## US-016: Preserve Hermes cancellation and timeout handling

Date: 2026-11-23
Status: BLOCKED on full-suite environment permissions

### What changed
- Added built-CLI regressions for SIGINT and SIGTERM cancellation.
  The fake records stdin EOF and waits for its descendant to record
  its own PID before signalling readiness. Cancellation must exit
  130/143 and kill both Hermes and the descendant holding stdout.
- Added a coordinated timeout case: fake Hermes commits work, leaves
  a dirty file and starts its descendant before signalling readiness.
  With a 15-second timeout, committed and dirty work both reach the
  real test gate and merge. One available retry must remain unused.
- Extended spawnCli with an optional child callback and deadline for
  lifecycle tests. Existing callers retain their defaults. Both fake
  environment key lists include the new controls.
- Kept production process groups, registries, timeout classification,
  auto-commit policy and src/index.ts signal handlers unchanged.

### Test-first evidence and patterns
- Wrote the cancellation and timeout regressions first. Both failed
  because the fake lacked the requested descendant coordination;
  implemented the fake modes afterward and observed both pass.
- Readiness contains the agent PID and is emitted only after the child
  records its PID. Tests wait on conditions rather than fixed sleeps.
- Cleanup signals the CLI first, waits for it, then uses the existing
  process-group helper and removes worktrees and temporary files.
- docs/INDEX.md is absent; studied docs/README.md as the available
  documentation entry point. No new dependencies were needed.

